cryption Function**\n\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/crypto.py` (lines 43-48)\n\n```python\ndef decrypt(ciphertext: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Decrypt ciphertext. Returns None if invalid/corrupted.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return _get_fernet().decrypt(ciphertext.encode()).decode()\n    except (InvalidToken, Exception):\n        return None\n```\n\n### **Encryption Flow (When Passwords Stored)**\n\n**File:** `/home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/api/routers/manager_api.py` (line 1959)\n\nPasswords are encrypted when storing accounts via the Manager API:\n\n```python\nfrom core.crypto import encrypt as _encrypt_password\nencrypted_pw = _encrypt_password(payload.password)\nacct[\"password_encrypted\"] = encrypted_pw\n```\n\n### **Password Storage Patterns in resources.yaml**\n\nTwo formats are supported:\n\n1. **Inline (per-account)** — stored directly in YAML:\n   ```yaml\n   servers:\n     server-name:\n       accounts:\n         - name: account-1\n           user: root\n           password_encrypted: \"gAAAAABqA9GXA_Jhf931uY_...\"  # Fernet ciphertext\n   ```\n\n2. **Legacy (per-server file)** — stored separately:\n   ```\n   config/server_passwords/<server>.enc  # File contains encrypted password\n   ```\n\n### **Key Security Characteristics**\n\n- ✅ **No plaintext persistence** — passwords are immediately encrypted on receipt\n- ✅ **No external key files required** — key derived from machine MAC\n- ✅ **Machine-bound security** — ciphertext only decrypts on the original machine\n- ✅ **Mode 0600 protection** — encrypted files stored with restrictive permissions\n- ⚠️ **Not suitable for distributed secrets** — tied to single machine's UUID"
